# CITATION

When using the TRCSS software or results in published work, please cite:

**Manuscript (NAR Methods submission):**
> TRCSS Contributors (2026). "TRCSS: Transcription-Replication Context Score
> for Improved Prime Editing Efficiency Prediction." *Nucleic Acids Research
> Methods*. Submitted. DOI: PENDING.

**Software archive:**
> TRCSS Contributors (2026). *TRCSS v1.0.0-submission*. Zenodo.
> https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.XXXXX

For BibTeX entries see [CITATION.cff](CITATION.cff) or `README.md`.

---

**Underlying datasets.** If you rely on the 146-site arrayed validation panel,
additionally cite the original source:
> Mathis N, Allam A, Kissling L, et al. (2025). Machine learning prediction of
> prime editing efficiency across diverse chromatin contexts. *Nature
> Biotechnology*, 43(5):712–719. Data: GEO GSE270866 (CC BY 4.0).
